  "notes": [
    "Dry propulsion is counted once here and removed from the ACS aggregate.",
    "The loaded propellant allowance is copied from the workbook. It is a launch-mass heuristic, not a delta-v prediction. Set parameters.sizingMode to rocketEquation after entering delta-v and specific impulse to replace it with a calculated load.",
    "Translational delta-v and rotational rates are separate inputs. No trajectory, torque allocation, minimum impulse bit or plume model is solved.",
    "Tank and pressurization candidates roll up their own mass and power. The baseline TBD choices use includedInPackage:true and are covered by the dry package. If a group is itemized, the combined package allowance becomes TBD to avoid counting that hardware twice. Enter a core-hardware option with includesGroups:[] after separating the package. No source split is invented.",
    "The source propellant allowance is held at its workbook cached value until edited or replaced by rocket-equation sizing. It does not rescale with mirror geometry."
